      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <float.h>\n\n// Max-heap node (1-indexed)\ntypedef struct {\n    float dist;\n    char label;\n} HeapNode;\n\nstatic inline void heap_swap(HeapNode *a, HeapNode *b) {\n    HeapNode t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t;\n}\n\n// Sift down from index idx in a max-heap of size heap_size (1-indexed)\nstatic inline void sift_down(HeapNode *heap, int heap_size, int idx) {\n    while (1) {\n        int largest = idx;\n        int left = 2 * idx;\n        int right = 2 * idx + 1;\n        if (left <= heap_size && heap[left].dist > heap[largest].dist)\n            largest = left;\n        if (right <= heap_size && heap[right].dist > heap[largest].dist)\n            largest = right;\n        if (largest == idx) break;\n        heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[largest]);\n        idx = largest;\n    }\n}\n\n// Insert or replace in a max-heap of capacity k.\nstatic inline void heap_insert_or_replace(float d, char label,\n                                          HeapNode *heap, int *heap_size_ptr, int k) {\n    int hs = *heap_size_ptr;\n    if (hs < k) {\n        // Insert at end and bubble up\n        hs++;\n        int idx = hs;\n        heap[idx].dist = d;\n        heap[idx].label = label;\n        while (idx > 1 && heap[idx / 2].dist < heap[idx].dist) {\n            heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[idx / 2]);\n            idx /= 2;\n        }\n    } else if (d < heap[1].dist) {\n        // Replace root\n        heap[1].dist = d;\n        heap[1].label = label;\n        sift_down(heap, k, 1);\n    }\n    *heap_size_ptr = hs;\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    // Hoist query coordinates outside parallel region (B)\n    const float tx = to_evaluate.x;\n    const float ty = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    int max_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\n    if (max_threads < 1) max_threads = 1;\n\n    // Per-thread heaps: each thread gets a heap array of size k+1 and its current size.\n    HeapNode **thread_heaps = (HeapNode**) malloc(max_threads * sizeof(HeapNode*));\n    int *thread_sizes = (int*) calloc(max_threads, sizeof(int));\n\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\n        thread_heaps[t] = (HeapNode*) malloc((k + 1) * sizeof(HeapNode));\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        HeapNode *local_heap = thread_heaps[tid];\n        int local_size = 0;\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\n            Group g = groups[gi];\n            float * restrict xs = g.xs;\n            float * restrict ys = g.ys;\n            int len = g.length;\n            char label = g.label;\n\n            // Process points in batches of 16 using NEON SIMD with prefetching (B)\n            int j = 0;\n            for (; j + 15 < len; j += 16) {\n                __builtin_prefetch(xs + j + 32);\n                __builtin_prefetch(ys + j + 24);\n\n                float32x4x4_t x_vec_quad = vld1q_f32_x4(xs + j);\n                float32x4x4_t y_vec_quad = vld1q_f32_x4(ys + j);\n\n                // Compute distances for each of the four vectors\n                float32x4_t dx0 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[0], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy0 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[0], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq0 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx0, dx0), dy0, dy0);\n\n                float32x4_t dx1 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[1], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy1 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[1], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq1 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx1, dx1), dy1, dy1);\n\n                float32x4_t dx2 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[2], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy2 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[2], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq2 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx2, dx2), dy2, dy2);\n\n                float32x4_t dx3 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[3], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy3 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[3], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq3 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx3, dx3), dy3, dy3);\n\n                // Store all 16 distances\n                float d[16];\n                vst1q_f32(d,     dist_sq0);\n                vst1q_f32(d + 4, dist_sq1);\n                vst1q_f32(d + 8, dist_sq2);\n                vst1q_f32(d+12, dist_sq3);\n\n                // Insert all 16 distances into heap (A: direct iteration without copying)\n                for (int t = 0; t < 16; t++) {\n                    heap_insert_or_replace(d[t], label, local_heap, &local_size, k);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Scalar remainder with prefetching and NEON batch of 4 (B)\n            for (; j + 3 < len; j += 4) {\n                __builtin_prefetch(xs + j + 8);\n                __builtin_prefetch(ys + j + 6);\n\n                float32x4_t x_vec = vld1q_f32(xs + j);\n                float32x4_t y_vec = vld1q_f32(ys + j);\n\n                float32x4_t dx = vsubq_f32(x_vec, vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy = vsubq_f32(y_vec, vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx, dx), dy, dy);\n\n                float d[4];\n                vst1q_f32(d, dist_sq);\n                for (int t = 0; t < 4; t++) {\n                    heap_insert_or_replace(d[t], label, local_heap, &local_size, k);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Final scalar remainder\n            for (; j < len; j++) {\n                float dx = xs[j] - tx;\n                float dy = ys[j] - ty;\n                float d = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n                heap_insert_or_replace(d, label, local_heap, &local_size, k);\n            }\n        }\n\n        thread_sizes[tid] = local_size;\n    }\n\n    // Global max-heap to merge per-thread results (C: parallel with per-thread heaps)\n    HeapNode *global_heap = (HeapNode*) malloc((k + 1) * sizeof(HeapNode));\n    int global_size = 0;\n\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\n        HeapNode *local = thread_heaps[t];\n        int sz = thread_sizes[t];\n        if (sz > k) sz = k;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= sz; i++) {\n            heap_insert_or_replace(local[i].dist, local[i].label,\n                                   global_heap, &global_size, k);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Extract labels from final global heap\n    char *labels = (char*) malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n    int actual_k = (global_size < k) ? global_size : k;\n    for (int i = 0; i < actual_k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = global_heap[i + 1].label;\n    }\n    for (int i = actual_k; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    free(global_heap);\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\n        free(thread_heaps[t]);\n    }\n    free(thread_heaps);\n    free(thread_sizes);\n\n    // Find most frequent label using frequency array (A: replace qsort)\n    int freq[256] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        freq[(unsigned char)labels[i]]++;\n    }\n\n    char best_label = labels[0];\n    int best_count = freq[(unsigned char)best_label];\n    for (int c = 1; c < 256; c++) {\n        if (freq[c] > best_count) {\n            best_count = freq[c];\n            best_label = (char)c;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(labels);\n    return best_label;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; ++i) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    },
    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float x;\n    float y;\n} Point;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n    float * restrict xs;   // array of x coordinates (B: restrict qualifier)\n    float * restrict ys;   // array of y coordinates\n} Group;\n\nvoid on_error() {\n    printf(\"Invalid input file.\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\" n_groups=%d \", &n) != 1) on_error();\n    return n;\n}\n\nPoint parse_point() {\n    float x, y;\n    if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2) on_error();\n    Point point;\n    point.x = x;\n    point.y = y;\n    return point;\n}\n\nGroup parse_next_group() {\n    char label; \n    int length;\n\n    if (scanf(\" label=%c \", &label) != 1) on_error();\n    if (scanf(\" length=%d \", &length) != 1) on_error();\n\n    Group group;\n    group.label = label;\n    group.length = length;\n    group.xs = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * length);\n    group.ys = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * length);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        Point p = parse_point();\n        group.xs[i] = p.x;\n        group.ys[i] = p.y;\n    }\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nint parse_k() {\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\" k=%d \", &k) != 1) on_error();\n    return k;\n}\n\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\n    float dx = b.x - a.x;\n    float dy = b.y - a.y;\n    return dx * dx + dy * dy;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.h"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating all three archived transformations: (A) max-heap top-k selection with frequency-array counting and direct iteration over groups without copying, (B) hoisted query coordinates outside inner loops, software prefetching for xs/ys arrays, restrict qualifiers on Group pointer members, and NEON SIMD distance computation using batch size 16 via vld1q_f32_x4 plus a scalar remainder with batch-4 NEON, and (C) OpenMP parallelization over groups with per-thread max-heaps allocated once outside the parallel region and static scheduling will yield a correct program that is faster than any single transformation. The combination reduces memory latency through prefetching, eliminates redundant coordinate loads, exploits SIMD parallelism for distance computation, and distributes work across threads without synchronization during insertion.",
  "notes": "The current source already incorporated many elements from previous integrations; this version adds explicit software prefetching (B), hoists query coordinates to the top of knn() (B), uses restrict qualifiers on xs/ys in both struct definition and local pointers (B), retains per-thread max-heaps with global heap merge (C), and keeps frequency-array final selection (A). The scalar remainder loop now also processes batches of 4 using NEON vld1q_f32 for additional SIMD coverage. All three source ideas are fully represented.",
